Most managed starter websites are live within 5–7 days of us receiving your details. Here's how that process works — what happens at each stage and what we need from you.

## Step 1: You tell us about your business

We'll ask for the basics: what you do, where you work, who your customers are, and any existing branding — logo, colours, photos. The more you can give us upfront, the faster we can move.

Don't worry if you don't have professional photos or polished copy. We draft the content around what you tell us, then get your approval before anything goes live.

## Step 2: We build the site

Using our streamlined build process, we put together a professional, branded website structured properly for Google — correct page titles, headings, descriptions, and a clean layout that works on mobile and desktop.

We register your domain, set up hosting, and configure SSL. By the time you see the site, the technical foundations are already in place.

## Step 3: You review it

We send you a preview link before going live. You check the content, the look, and anything you want adjusted. We make the changes, and once you're happy, the site goes live.

## Step 4: Ongoing management

After launch, we handle everything in the background — daily backups, security updates, technical maintenance. Each month, we add the number of new pages included in your plan.

You choose what those pages cover — new services, locations you work in, questions your customers ask — or we recommend topics based on what people in your area are searching for.

## What you don't need to do

No hosting accounts. No domain registrar logins. No plugin updates. No worrying about whether the site is secure. That's all handled as part of the plan.

[Find out more about our managed starter websites](/services/managed-starter-websites/) or [get in touch to get started](/contact/).
